## SCOPE (disclosed)

`theo:universality_tori` holds in corrected forms only, unmarked. Readings: the two generators of
l.293 and l.1022 are `S = [[0,-1],[1,0]]`, `T = [[1,1],[0,1]]` (any set of moves whose linear
parts generate `SL_d(ℤ)` is covered by `universality_tori_sl`); "their inverse" are the moves with
linear parts `S⁻¹`, `T⁻¹` and translations of their own (exact inverses are a special case); the
"2 elements of `SL_d(ℤ)`" of l.440 are `S`, `T` (the harness, C-34), both counts (12, 20) proved.
Mathlib's Fourier lemmas use `haarAddCircle` through a local `MeasureSpace`; it is the global
`volume` (`volume_unitAddTorus_eq_pi_haar`). Not proved: the two-generation of `SL_d(ℤ)`,
`d ≥ 3`, and its free subgroups (l.821); neither is needed. Nothing ported from GFNBounds.

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`.
